1
00:00:13,993 --> 00:00:17,038
OUR STICKY LOVE

2
00:00:54,367 --> 00:00:55,994
This is so nice.

3
00:00:56,077 --> 00:00:57,245
That's right!

4
00:00:57,328 --> 00:00:59,831
Today's your birthday.
Is there anything you want to do?

5
00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:02,292
I never thought about it.

6
00:01:03,960 --> 00:01:05,211
Want to go see my family?

7
00:01:06,671 --> 00:01:07,755
What?

8
00:01:07,839 --> 00:01:09,174
I have family too.

9
00:01:10,008 --> 00:01:12,719
A grandmother who accepts me
without any questions.

10
00:01:12,802 --> 00:01:14,304
I just asked my family to return.

11
00:01:14,387 --> 00:01:15,972
Do you have a problem with that?

12
00:01:17,891 --> 00:01:20,310
Sisters who always have my back.

13
00:01:20,393 --> 00:01:22,604
I was your closest friend in the village.

14
00:01:22,687 --> 00:01:25,481
A friend with the purest of hearts, and a…

15
00:01:25,565 --> 00:01:26,941
Slightly older brother-in-law.

16
00:01:27,025 --> 00:01:29,903
A slightly older brother-in-law.

17
00:01:31,279 --> 00:01:33,573
You can ask me to run errands
as much as you want.

18
00:01:33,656 --> 00:01:35,867
And a dutiful younger brother.

19
00:01:36,701 --> 00:01:39,746
I miss them all so much.

20
00:01:47,045 --> 00:01:48,129
This is nice.

21
00:02:03,228 --> 00:02:07,440
I'll have grilled whole potatoes,
sausage, and rice cake skewers.

22
00:02:07,523 --> 00:02:08,733
What about you?

23
00:02:10,777 --> 00:02:13,154
Oppa, come here.

24
00:02:16,866 --> 00:02:18,201
Oppa, should we get coffee?

25
00:02:18,993 --> 00:02:20,411
I want an iced mocha. You?

26
00:02:21,621 --> 00:02:23,957
Oppa, do you have a hole in your chin?

27
00:02:24,457 --> 00:02:25,625
This is really good.

28
00:02:26,167 --> 00:02:27,252
Oppa, say "ah."

29
00:02:29,420 --> 00:02:30,255
Oppa, you okay?

30
00:02:33,591 --> 00:02:34,425
Jang Tae-ha.

31
00:02:34,509 --> 00:02:35,677
Yeah?

32
00:02:35,760 --> 00:02:37,303
I asked what you're going to eat.

33
00:02:38,263 --> 00:02:40,807
Right. I'll have what you're having.

34
00:02:41,683 --> 00:02:45,144
Two butter-grilled potatoes,
two sausage and rice cake skewers, please.

35
00:02:46,229 --> 00:02:47,522
Here, look at this.

36
00:02:47,605 --> 00:02:49,315
-Goodness, ma'am!
-Why?

37
00:02:50,483 --> 00:02:52,527
-Ma'am.
-Did you go grocery shopping?

38
00:02:52,610 --> 00:02:53,778
Yes.

39
00:02:54,570 --> 00:02:56,572
It's Tae-ha's birthday today.

40
00:02:56,656 --> 00:02:58,574
Wait. Is that so?

41
00:02:58,658 --> 00:02:59,492
Yes.

42
00:02:59,575 --> 00:03:02,537
That's right. Tae-ha's birthday
was around this time of year.

43
00:03:02,620 --> 00:03:04,831
-You're right.
-Today's his birthday.

44
00:03:05,873 --> 00:03:08,668
Oh, I see you're all here.
Jeong-hwa is back.

45
00:03:08,751 --> 00:03:10,295
-Careful.
-Jeong…

46
00:03:10,378 --> 00:03:12,380
-Jeong-hwa.
-Hello.

47
00:03:12,463 --> 00:03:14,007
-I'm back.
-Jeong-hwa.

48
00:03:14,090 --> 00:03:16,134
-Are you feeling better?
-Yes.

49
00:03:16,217 --> 00:03:17,719
While I was hospitalized,

50
00:03:17,802 --> 00:03:20,847
we got to spend time glued to each other,
like newlyweds again.

51
00:03:20,930 --> 00:03:24,183
Thank goodness
the car accident wasn't worse.

52
00:03:24,267 --> 00:03:25,476
-Exactly.
-Yes.

53
00:03:25,560 --> 00:03:29,188
It's Tae-ha's birthday today,
so we hurried over here.

54
00:03:29,772 --> 00:03:32,066
Ma'am, I'll help you with the food later.

55
00:03:32,150 --> 00:03:35,028
-Goodness, no.
-You don't need to help.

56
00:03:35,111 --> 00:03:36,154
We'll help out.

57
00:03:36,237 --> 00:03:38,448
-I'm fine.
-You should rest.

58
00:03:39,198 --> 00:03:41,200
I'll help out too!

59
00:03:44,704 --> 00:03:45,580
Eun-sae!

60
00:03:46,956 --> 00:03:48,750
-Grandma!
-Oh, yes. Goodness me.

61
00:03:48,833 --> 00:03:51,461
Good heavens, what's happening?

62
00:03:51,544 --> 00:03:53,421
Goodness, you're here.

63
00:03:54,047 --> 00:03:55,214
Ms. Prosecutor.

64
00:03:56,549 --> 00:03:59,886
I thought I was Tae-ha's wife here,
not a prosecutor.

65
00:03:59,969 --> 00:04:01,387
What's going on?

66
00:04:01,471 --> 00:04:04,474
I thought you'd never come here again.

67
00:04:04,557 --> 00:04:06,392
That's impossible.

68
00:04:08,478 --> 00:04:09,729
Because our connection…

69
00:04:13,775 --> 00:04:15,318
is like taffy.

70
00:04:15,401 --> 00:04:17,779
That's right.

71
00:04:18,654 --> 00:04:20,073
Welcome back.

72
00:04:20,156 --> 00:04:22,241
-Ladies.
-Welcome back.

73
00:04:25,703 --> 00:04:27,705
-I missed you.
-Me too.

74
00:04:27,789 --> 00:04:30,625
Well done for coming back.

75
00:04:30,708 --> 00:04:32,377
We only got to see you on TV.

76
00:04:32,460 --> 00:04:35,463
Happy birthday to you

77
00:04:35,546 --> 00:04:38,466
Happy birthday to you

78
00:04:38,549 --> 00:04:41,928
Happy birthday dear Jang Tae-ha

79
00:04:42,011 --> 00:04:44,806
Happy birthday to you

80
00:04:47,016 --> 00:04:48,643
-Make a wish.
-Go on.

81
00:04:50,645 --> 00:04:51,896
We can hear you.

82
00:04:51,979 --> 00:04:53,106
He's like a kid.

83
00:04:58,820 --> 00:05:00,488
-Happy birthday!
-Happy birthday.

84
00:05:00,571 --> 00:05:01,406
Happy birthday.

85
00:05:01,489 --> 00:05:02,490
Happy birthday.

86
00:05:02,573 --> 00:05:04,492
Thank you all so much.

87
00:05:05,451 --> 00:05:07,161
Tae-ha, is there anything you want?

88
00:05:07,245 --> 00:05:08,704
It'll be our treat.

89
00:05:08,788 --> 00:05:10,581
Come on, Hui-ja.

90
00:05:10,665 --> 00:05:12,291
What could we possibly give him

91
00:05:12,375 --> 00:05:14,877
that would compare to the gift
he already received?

92
00:05:14,961 --> 00:05:15,920
That's true.

93
00:05:17,171 --> 00:05:19,173
His fake bride has become his real bride.

94
00:05:19,257 --> 00:05:21,175
What gift could possibly top that?

95
00:05:21,259 --> 00:05:23,344
Oh, come on.

96
00:05:23,845 --> 00:05:26,722
You two sure took the long way around.

97
00:05:27,849 --> 00:05:31,602
Now all that's left is for them to live
happily ever after like us.

98
00:05:36,983 --> 00:05:38,234
Now that I think about it,

99
00:05:38,317 --> 00:05:40,153
they're the spitting image.

100
00:05:40,778 --> 00:05:41,612
Sorry?

101
00:05:41,696 --> 00:05:42,697
Who is?

102
00:05:43,281 --> 00:05:46,617
Her and Tae-ha's mom.

103
00:05:47,118 --> 00:05:47,952
Sorry?

104
00:05:48,619 --> 00:05:50,288
Me and Tae-ha's mother?

105
00:05:57,879 --> 00:06:01,048
32 YEARS AGO

106
00:06:04,343 --> 00:06:05,219
Are your feet cold?

107
00:06:07,763 --> 00:06:09,098
How pretty.

108
00:06:09,765 --> 00:06:14,896
Along the fruit farm path
Outside the village

109
00:06:15,521 --> 00:06:19,400
The African flowers are in full bloom

110
00:06:20,943 --> 00:06:22,570
Isn't it "acacia"?

111
00:06:23,154 --> 00:06:23,988
Pardon?

112
00:06:27,617 --> 00:06:28,868
Acacia.

113
00:06:31,412 --> 00:06:33,206
Acacia.

114
00:06:39,587 --> 00:06:42,423
You look like you're from out of town,
not from Gujin.

115
00:06:42,507 --> 00:06:43,841
That's right.

116
00:06:43,925 --> 00:06:47,428
I came after hearing about a dishwashing
job that came with room and board,

117
00:06:47,512 --> 00:06:49,222
but they already hired someone.

118
00:06:51,432 --> 00:06:52,433
How old?

119
00:06:52,517 --> 00:06:54,560
Six months.

120
00:06:55,269 --> 00:06:56,270
No, I meant…

121
00:07:17,041 --> 00:07:20,086
There's a sink full of dishes
back at my place too.

122
00:07:22,547 --> 00:07:25,591
I guess you could stay with me tonight
if you have nowhere else to go.

123
00:07:41,023 --> 00:07:41,983
What are you doing?

124
00:07:42,066 --> 00:07:45,361
Don't stand around.
Lay him in there and get him comfy.

125
00:07:49,156 --> 00:07:49,991
Thank you.

126
00:08:06,299 --> 00:08:08,884
The sunset is so pretty from here!

127
00:08:09,385 --> 00:08:12,555
It's so spectacle.

128
00:08:13,598 --> 00:08:14,849
"Spectacular."

129
00:08:21,105 --> 00:08:24,942
I was planning on going to night school
once the baby's a bit older.

130
00:08:28,029 --> 00:08:30,740
You don't look that old yourself, lady.

131
00:08:30,823 --> 00:08:32,700
I'm 23.

132
00:08:33,200 --> 00:08:35,161
So I'm technically a young lady.

133
00:08:36,996 --> 00:08:38,372
I guess so.

134
00:08:41,459 --> 00:08:44,503
My daughter would be your age
if she were still alive.

135
00:08:47,673 --> 00:08:48,841
And the baby's dad?

136
00:08:50,593 --> 00:08:52,720
He's not around.
I'm raising him on my own.

137
00:08:53,554 --> 00:08:54,847
No parents to rely on?

138
00:08:55,765 --> 00:08:56,599
None.

139
00:08:57,475 --> 00:08:58,934
That's why I'm four in one.

140
00:08:59,560 --> 00:09:03,272
His grandma, grandpa, and dad.
I'll be everything for him.

141
00:09:05,024 --> 00:09:08,235
A baby doesn't need a smart mom
who went to college.

142
00:09:08,903 --> 00:09:11,280
The best mom is one
who showers her baby with love.

143
00:09:17,495 --> 00:09:20,498
I'll cook dinner today to repay you
for letting us stay the night.

144
00:09:20,581 --> 00:09:23,125
Well, if you say so.

145
00:09:31,550 --> 00:09:32,802
Please try it.

146
00:09:38,683 --> 00:09:41,018
Golly, you make a mean gochujang stew.

147
00:09:41,102 --> 00:09:42,645
Where did you learn to make this?

148
00:09:43,437 --> 00:09:45,731
I've just made it a lot.

149
00:09:46,232 --> 00:09:47,483
Because someone likes it.

150
00:09:53,489 --> 00:09:55,241
Didn't you say you're four in one?

151
00:09:55,783 --> 00:09:59,537
You should eat four times as much
so you have the energy to raise your baby.

152
00:10:01,622 --> 00:10:05,334
No one really knows
how my Tae-ha's life will turn out.

153
00:10:06,127 --> 00:10:07,920
Just look at The Last Match.

154
00:10:08,003 --> 00:10:09,964
It looks like
Son Ji-chang's team will win,

155
00:10:10,047 --> 00:10:13,008
but in the end,
Jang Dong-gun makes a dunk,

156
00:10:13,092 --> 00:10:14,593
and his team wins.

157
00:10:15,177 --> 00:10:17,346
Life is like a basketball game.

158
00:10:17,430 --> 00:10:20,391
My Tae-ha may not have the best luck
when it comes to parents,

159
00:10:20,474 --> 00:10:23,477
but who knows if he'll throw down
a huge dunk later in life?

160
00:10:25,187 --> 00:10:26,731
Who says he's unlucky?

161
00:10:27,565 --> 00:10:29,775
Look at those chubby cheeks of his.

162
00:10:29,859 --> 00:10:32,611
They're so chubby,
they might burst any minute.

163
00:10:33,571 --> 00:10:37,366
You're like a skewer,
and yet you've fed him so well.

164
00:10:37,950 --> 00:10:39,744
You can search all over the country.

165
00:10:39,827 --> 00:10:41,912
There aren't many mothers
as admirable as you.

166
00:10:45,124 --> 00:10:46,959
I'm admirable?

167
00:10:47,042 --> 00:10:47,918
Of course.

168
00:10:48,002 --> 00:10:51,464
With no one to rely on, you still
protected your child with all your might.

169
00:10:51,547 --> 00:10:53,758
If you're not an admirable mother, who is?

170
00:10:57,636 --> 00:10:58,971
If you have nowhere to go,

171
00:10:59,555 --> 00:11:02,016
do you want to just stay here
and make taffy with me?

172
00:11:06,145 --> 00:11:06,979
Really?

173
00:11:07,897 --> 00:11:10,441
I'll even throw your baby
a great first birthday party.

174
00:11:15,654 --> 00:11:16,739
Hurry and eat up.

175
00:11:20,493 --> 00:11:23,412
Goodness, I doubt
you're even eating regular meals.

176
00:11:23,496 --> 00:11:24,914
Here, have some hairtail.

177
00:11:24,997 --> 00:11:26,999
HAPPY FIRST BIRTHDAY

178
00:11:27,082 --> 00:11:30,544
The baby is the star of the show.
Why would I dress up?

179
00:11:30,628 --> 00:11:32,004
Please hold still.

180
00:11:32,087 --> 00:11:35,716
A first birthday photo is forever.
His grandma should be pretty.

181
00:11:36,842 --> 00:11:38,052
There.

182
00:11:38,552 --> 00:11:40,429
-That's enough.
-All done.

183
00:11:41,430 --> 00:11:42,389
All right.

184
00:11:42,932 --> 00:11:43,808
Okay.

185
00:11:44,308 --> 00:11:46,185
Let's see what our Tae-ha will pick.

186
00:11:46,268 --> 00:11:47,645
-All right.
-What's your pick?

187
00:11:47,728 --> 00:11:51,273
Okay, Tae-ha.
Which one of these takes your fancy?

188
00:11:51,357 --> 00:11:52,650
Let's grab one.

189
00:11:52,733 --> 00:11:54,360
Good boy. The gavel.

190
00:11:54,443 --> 00:11:56,195
Grab the gavel. Go on.

191
00:11:56,278 --> 00:11:57,738
That's it. Good boy.

192
00:12:00,616 --> 00:12:05,287
She lived a lonely life without any
belongings in the world to call her own,

193
00:12:05,371 --> 00:12:08,040
and yet she never lost heart
and stayed so bright.

194
00:12:10,918 --> 00:12:15,548
And just like a certain someone,
she hated being called "lady."

195
00:12:16,674 --> 00:12:20,928
Seeing you with such a good person
and being so affectionate with her…

196
00:12:22,054 --> 00:12:24,056
I'm sure Tae-ha's mom is smiling

197
00:12:24,932 --> 00:12:25,891
way up there.

198
00:12:26,392 --> 00:12:27,643
Yes.

199
00:12:28,352 --> 00:12:30,145
She's probably smiling with happiness.

200
00:12:30,646 --> 00:12:33,107
-I'm sure she is.
-Yes.

201
00:12:33,190 --> 00:12:35,818
Tae-ha's mom, thank you for the food!

202
00:12:36,360 --> 00:12:37,611
Thank you for the food!

203
00:12:38,737 --> 00:12:40,197
-Let's eat.
-Please eat.

204
00:12:41,115 --> 00:12:43,450
Ma'am, when are you going back to Seoul?

205
00:12:48,414 --> 00:12:49,957
I have to leave soon.

206
00:12:50,040 --> 00:12:52,251
-You're leaving already?
-So soon?

207
00:12:52,334 --> 00:12:54,837
It's not even taffy-making day today,

208
00:12:54,920 --> 00:12:58,757
but I guess the whole village
will smell sickly sweet later.

209
00:12:58,841 --> 00:13:00,759
Oh my goodness!

210
00:13:03,137 --> 00:13:05,055
I told you I'd drive you to Seoul.

211
00:13:05,639 --> 00:13:07,766
I told you I don't want to hassle you.

212
00:13:08,350 --> 00:13:09,810
I told you, I'm fine.

213
00:13:09,894 --> 00:13:12,187
And I told you, I'm really fine.

214
00:13:25,117 --> 00:13:25,951
Just look at them.

215
00:13:27,411 --> 00:13:29,955
I'm going to miss you so much
until the weekend.

216
00:13:32,541 --> 00:13:33,459
Me too.

217
00:13:37,630 --> 00:13:38,464
Hold up.

218
00:13:39,298 --> 00:13:43,385
You said I was the one and only woman
in your life.

219
00:13:43,469 --> 00:13:45,804
Does that mean
this is your first real relationship?

220
00:13:45,888 --> 00:13:49,266
-Yes, he's been single since birth.
-It's his first.

221
00:13:51,310 --> 00:13:53,604
So what if it's my first?

222
00:13:56,607 --> 00:13:58,442
Speaking from experience,

223
00:13:58,525 --> 00:14:01,028
starting tomorrow, people will look at you

224
00:14:01,111 --> 00:14:02,821
like you're a lunatic.

225
00:14:04,907 --> 00:14:07,159
-Looks delicious.
-It does.

226
00:14:17,294 --> 00:14:18,963
-Are you nuts?
-Sorry?

227
00:14:19,046 --> 00:14:21,882
Even an Olympic gold medalist
wouldn't smile as wide as you.

228
00:14:27,054 --> 00:14:28,305
So this is what she meant.

229
00:14:31,308 --> 00:14:32,726
And suddenly,

230
00:14:32,810 --> 00:14:35,646
everything in the world
will look beautiful.

231
00:14:35,729 --> 00:14:37,982
What are you doing? What are you saying?

232
00:14:38,065 --> 00:14:39,358
Hey, Tae-ha!

233
00:14:39,858 --> 00:14:41,151
-Hello.
-Hi.

234
00:14:43,112 --> 00:14:44,780
-A bird pooped on him.
-Bird poop?

235
00:14:44,863 --> 00:14:46,073
-Yeah.
-Oh dear.

236
00:14:47,783 --> 00:14:49,284
That's what bird poop looks like?

237
00:14:49,868 --> 00:14:50,911
Is he smiling?

238
00:14:51,412 --> 00:14:53,664
What, is he that bird expert, Yun Mu-bu?

239
00:14:53,747 --> 00:14:56,834
Why is he looking so lovingly
at bird poop?

240
00:14:58,127 --> 00:15:01,130
Try giving him cow or dog poop.

241
00:15:01,213 --> 00:15:05,217
Right now, even a field of poop
will look like a field of flowers to him.

242
00:15:06,301 --> 00:15:07,928
-Look at this.
-Look at what?

243
00:15:08,012 --> 00:15:09,513
What bird do you think did this?

244
00:15:09,596 --> 00:15:11,140
-Stay away!
-What the heck?

245
00:15:11,640 --> 00:15:15,644
And you'll feel a new sense of gratitude
for the invention of cell phones.

246
00:15:16,186 --> 00:15:19,773
I feel like I can finally breathe,
seeing your face like this.

247
00:15:20,399 --> 00:15:22,735
How did people
from the Goryeo and Joseon periods

248
00:15:22,818 --> 00:15:24,737
endure their lovesickness without phones?

249
00:15:24,820 --> 00:15:26,488
Maybe that's why they died so young.

250
00:15:29,366 --> 00:15:30,784
We'll finally meet up tomorrow.

251
00:15:31,285 --> 00:15:35,456
Yeah. I'm going to stick to you like glue
all day tomorrow.

252
00:15:36,457 --> 00:15:38,625
By the way, what should we

253
00:15:38,709 --> 00:15:39,918
call each other?

254
00:15:40,586 --> 00:15:41,628
-Call each other?
-Yes.

255
00:15:41,712 --> 00:15:44,339
It feels a bit too formal
always calling you "Jang Tae-ha."

256
00:15:46,425 --> 00:15:47,426
Oppa.

257
00:15:48,594 --> 00:15:50,763
Oppa, do you have a hole in your chin?

258
00:15:50,846 --> 00:15:51,847
Oppa, say "ah."

259
00:15:51,930 --> 00:15:52,806
Oppa, you okay?

260
00:15:57,728 --> 00:15:58,729
"Oppa"

261
00:15:59,855 --> 00:16:01,190
is a bit too cliché.

262
00:16:03,233 --> 00:16:06,195
Right. I think so too.

263
00:16:07,404 --> 00:16:08,614
What else is there?

264
00:16:09,406 --> 00:16:11,200
Just call me anything.

265
00:16:11,283 --> 00:16:13,077
I don't care what we call each other.

266
00:16:14,578 --> 00:16:15,454
Really?

267
00:16:15,954 --> 00:16:17,581
Well, okay.

268
00:16:17,664 --> 00:16:19,166
I'll pick you up tomorrow.

269
00:16:20,042 --> 00:16:20,918
Okay.

270
00:16:21,710 --> 00:16:25,172
I'll look so good tomorrow
that I'll blow you away. Just you wait.

271
00:16:57,412 --> 00:16:59,540
Jang Tae-ha.

272
00:17:01,625 --> 00:17:03,335
I missed you.

273
00:17:03,919 --> 00:17:04,753
Me too.

274
00:17:05,796 --> 00:17:09,049
Let's have lots of fun this weekend.

275
00:17:09,133 --> 00:17:11,677
I worked all night yesterday to do that.

276
00:17:13,178 --> 00:17:16,306
I think you're still working hard.

277
00:17:19,434 --> 00:17:20,269
You mean my looks?

278
00:17:21,103 --> 00:17:22,104
Yeah.

279
00:17:23,063 --> 00:17:24,231
Let's hurry and go.

280
00:17:29,653 --> 00:17:31,155
I'll choose the music.

281
00:17:31,655 --> 00:17:32,489
Sure.

282
00:17:33,740 --> 00:17:37,870
It's been a while, so maybe we should
listen to my favorite g.o.d oppas.

283
00:17:39,413 --> 00:17:40,747
Your g.o.d oppas?

284
00:17:40,831 --> 00:17:41,790
Yes.

285
00:17:41,874 --> 00:17:43,625
What's wrong with my g.o.d oppas?

286
00:17:44,751 --> 00:17:46,253
Huh? Nothing.

287
00:17:46,920 --> 00:17:47,838
It's good to hear.

288
00:17:53,802 --> 00:17:54,887
"Oppa"…

289
00:17:56,930 --> 00:17:58,557
is a bit too cliché.

290
00:18:00,392 --> 00:18:02,769
Right. I think so too.

291
00:18:04,062 --> 00:18:07,608
Are we a year apart?

292
00:18:07,691 --> 00:18:11,445
Yes, I'm 33, and you're 34.

293
00:18:11,945 --> 00:18:12,779
Right.

294
00:18:19,411 --> 00:18:20,954
We're so old, aren't we?

295
00:18:21,830 --> 00:18:22,664
Yeah.

296
00:18:23,749 --> 00:18:26,793
But I'm a year older than you, huh?

297
00:18:30,339 --> 00:18:31,965
That's okay.

298
00:18:32,549 --> 00:18:33,800
Stay strong.

299
00:18:49,191 --> 00:18:51,818
And thumbs up, please. All right.

300
00:18:51,902 --> 00:18:53,820
Take the picture. Smile.

301
00:18:53,904 --> 00:18:55,155
That's good.

302
00:18:55,864 --> 00:18:57,866
-Let me see. Did it come out nice?
-Yeah.

303
00:18:59,117 --> 00:19:00,619
It looks good.

304
00:19:00,702 --> 00:19:02,162
Why are we taking pictures?

305
00:19:02,246 --> 00:19:05,040
I have to brag about my friendship
with the star prosecutor.

306
00:19:05,123 --> 00:19:09,461
You could even say that our clinic
produced said star prosecutor.

307
00:19:09,544 --> 00:19:10,379
Right?

308
00:19:10,879 --> 00:19:12,923
Yes, well, thank you.

309
00:19:13,423 --> 00:19:16,510
I probably got my memory back
thanks to your treatment.

310
00:19:18,262 --> 00:19:20,138
As if I'd fall for that.

311
00:19:20,222 --> 00:19:21,848
You remembered.

312
00:19:22,432 --> 00:19:23,517
You know,

313
00:19:24,017 --> 00:19:27,187
it's great that you remembered
and are going back to your old life,

314
00:19:27,271 --> 00:19:30,232
but I'm a little sad
that I won't be able to see you anymore.

315
00:19:30,732 --> 00:19:33,568
Sure, we won't be seeing each other
as doctor and patient,

316
00:19:33,652 --> 00:19:36,071
but our relationship is still precious.

317
00:19:36,154 --> 00:19:39,408
Going forward, I'll consider you my oppa.

318
00:19:39,950 --> 00:19:41,076
What?

319
00:19:43,078 --> 00:19:44,079
Why are you shocked?

320
00:19:45,789 --> 00:19:48,292
Then should we cut ties
because I'm done with treatment?

321
00:19:48,375 --> 00:19:50,252
Yeah, she can consider me her oppa.

322
00:19:50,335 --> 00:19:51,753
Bring it in.

323
00:19:57,926 --> 00:19:59,136
Eun-sae.

324
00:19:59,761 --> 00:20:00,887
Gi-jun oppa?

325
00:20:03,890 --> 00:20:05,350
Hey, that's not bad.

326
00:20:07,728 --> 00:20:09,271
Yeah, that's better.

327
00:20:12,858 --> 00:20:15,902
Isn't it so nice to be back here
after so long?

328
00:20:19,614 --> 00:20:21,700
What's wrong, Jang Tae-ha?

329
00:20:23,869 --> 00:20:25,120
Gi-jun and I

330
00:20:26,038 --> 00:20:26,913
are the same age.

331
00:20:26,997 --> 00:20:30,125
I know.
You two were high school classmates.

332
00:20:31,543 --> 00:20:34,129
Yeah, we were classmates.

333
00:20:38,592 --> 00:20:39,426
I'll get the car.

334
00:20:44,014 --> 00:20:45,349
So cute.

335
00:20:46,099 --> 00:20:47,809
How is he so adorable?

336
00:20:48,352 --> 00:20:52,314
Yesterday, he was all,
"I don't care what we call each other."

337
00:20:53,106 --> 00:20:55,108
Jang Tae-ha, let's go together.

338
00:20:59,321 --> 00:21:00,197
This is good.

339
00:21:01,281 --> 00:21:04,284
Isn't it hard going back and forth
between Taffy Village and Seoul?

340
00:21:04,368 --> 00:21:07,954
It's not hard at all.
All the people I want to see are here.

341
00:21:09,247 --> 00:21:11,291
We went to see someone I'd missed today.

342
00:21:11,917 --> 00:21:12,751
Really? Who?

343
00:21:13,335 --> 00:21:14,336
Gi-jun oppa.

344
00:21:16,129 --> 00:21:20,634
Gi-jun, as in Tae-ha's friend
who treated you?

345
00:21:20,717 --> 00:21:21,676
-Yes.
-I see.

346
00:21:21,760 --> 00:21:25,097
But since he's not treating me anymore,
he's not my doctor.

347
00:21:25,180 --> 00:21:26,473
That makes sense.

348
00:21:26,556 --> 00:21:27,766
That's right.

349
00:21:28,725 --> 00:21:30,769
If we're just talking about looks,

350
00:21:30,852 --> 00:21:33,438
I look older than you,
so I could be your oppa too.

351
00:21:33,980 --> 00:21:36,441
That's true. You're absolutely right.

352
00:21:36,525 --> 00:21:39,319
People who don't know us would think
you're my oppa.

353
00:21:39,403 --> 00:21:40,320
That's right.

354
00:21:40,404 --> 00:21:42,614
Should I just call you oppa then?

355
00:21:42,697 --> 00:21:44,825
Then should we try hearing it?

356
00:21:45,325 --> 00:21:47,327
Gang-rok oppa.

357
00:21:49,079 --> 00:21:50,080
I like that.

358
00:21:52,082 --> 00:21:54,543
What? Why are you getting up
in the middle of eating?

359
00:21:55,961 --> 00:21:56,795
To feed the dog.

360
00:21:58,004 --> 00:21:59,047
Dogs get hungry too.

361
00:22:00,215 --> 00:22:01,299
Come when you're done.

362
00:22:14,479 --> 00:22:15,439
Stop it.

363
00:22:15,522 --> 00:22:17,149
-Yeah.
-You'll make the kid cry.

364
00:22:17,232 --> 00:22:18,150
Did you notice?

365
00:22:18,233 --> 00:22:19,192
Of course we did!

366
00:22:19,276 --> 00:22:22,863
If you had gone on any longer,
you would have called me oppa too.

367
00:22:24,739 --> 00:22:28,869
I just love how that oppa
acts like a blushing teen. He's adorable.

368
00:22:30,704 --> 00:22:34,499
Go and cheer him up. I bet his insides
are more burnt than this scorched rice.

369
00:22:35,375 --> 00:22:37,627
-I'll be right back.
-You don't have to come back.

370
00:22:38,170 --> 00:22:40,589
How can he be such a fool?

371
00:22:40,672 --> 00:22:41,965
Fool. A total fool.

372
00:22:45,635 --> 00:22:46,803
Jang Tae-ha.

373
00:22:47,929 --> 00:22:49,848
Jang Tae-ha.

374
00:22:51,600 --> 00:22:54,352
How could you go home without me?

375
00:22:59,065 --> 00:23:00,650
I was worried Blessing might be hungry.

376
00:23:05,280 --> 00:23:07,157
Are you sulking right now, Jang Tae-ha?

377
00:23:07,240 --> 00:23:08,950
No! Me?

378
00:23:10,118 --> 00:23:13,330
Even someone riding the bullet train
could see you're sulking.

379
00:23:14,039 --> 00:23:14,873
I'm not though.

380
00:23:14,956 --> 00:23:16,124
You are though.

381
00:23:16,625 --> 00:23:18,293
Do you think I don't know you?

382
00:23:18,376 --> 00:23:20,504
I can tell just by your face, Jang Tae-ha.

383
00:23:22,339 --> 00:23:25,300
The whole "Jang Tae-ha" thing…

384
00:23:25,967 --> 00:23:27,260
Gi-jun is an oppa.

385
00:23:27,344 --> 00:23:30,430
Gang-rok is an oppa. Even g.o.d are oppas.
So why am I the only one…

386
00:23:34,392 --> 00:23:36,269
Well, forget it.

387
00:23:40,482 --> 00:23:43,235
You're really leaving me behind, babe?

388
00:23:49,115 --> 00:23:51,159
I'm asking if you're going alone.

389
00:23:51,243 --> 00:23:53,078
Babe.

390
00:24:06,841 --> 00:24:10,929
I can call anyone "oppa."
"Babe" is so much better.

391
00:24:11,429 --> 00:24:12,722
Don't you think, babe?

392
00:24:16,351 --> 00:24:17,185
Yeah.

393
00:24:20,188 --> 00:24:22,524
Did you want me to call you "oppa"
that badly?

394
00:24:22,607 --> 00:24:23,692
Tae-ha oppa.

395
00:24:24,192 --> 00:24:26,069
Oppa.

396
00:24:26,152 --> 00:24:27,237
Oh, stop it.

397
00:24:27,904 --> 00:24:28,738
Should I?

398
00:24:28,822 --> 00:24:32,409
Then should I call you Jang Tae-ha again?
And speak to you politely?

399
00:24:36,329 --> 00:24:38,665
Come on, oppa! Tae-ha oppa.

400
00:24:39,165 --> 00:24:42,043
Oppa.

401
00:24:42,127 --> 00:24:43,044
Babe.

402
00:24:43,128 --> 00:24:45,714
Babe.

403
00:24:45,797 --> 00:24:46,881
Seriously.

404
00:24:46,965 --> 00:24:48,300
Oh, come on.

405
00:24:48,800 --> 00:24:50,343
I mean, I like it, but…

406
00:24:50,427 --> 00:24:51,469
But?

407
00:24:54,055 --> 00:24:55,890
It really is home sweet home.

408
00:24:59,978 --> 00:25:01,062
But

409
00:25:02,480 --> 00:25:04,691
what should I call you?

410
00:25:06,359 --> 00:25:09,613
Do I keep calling you "Go Eun-sae"?

411
00:25:09,696 --> 00:25:12,949
What's wrong with that?
I like hearing that name so much.

412
00:25:14,075 --> 00:25:16,661
-Because your mother gave you that name?
-Yes, exactly.

413
00:25:18,496 --> 00:25:19,914
This is just my guess,

414
00:25:20,498 --> 00:25:25,503
but I think my mom dreamt of a pretty bird
when she was pregnant with me.

415
00:25:26,004 --> 00:25:26,880
That could be true.

416
00:25:26,963 --> 00:25:27,964
Right?

417
00:25:32,093 --> 00:25:35,680
I wonder why your mother
named you "Tae-ha."

418
00:25:37,682 --> 00:25:38,642
I don't know.

419
00:25:40,477 --> 00:25:43,063
Maybe she wanted me to become
a strong person

420
00:25:43,813 --> 00:25:46,358
who can embrace everything
like a big river.

421
00:25:53,031 --> 00:25:55,992
But embracing everything and being patient

422
00:25:56,534 --> 00:25:57,911
is really hard to do.

423
00:25:59,245 --> 00:26:04,209
I don't think she wanted her child
to just be strong.

424
00:26:12,425 --> 00:26:14,761
I want to ask her, but I can't.

425
00:26:18,807 --> 00:26:19,808
Where is your mother?

426
00:26:21,810 --> 00:26:24,437
She's in a place
overlooking the entire village.

427
00:26:27,524 --> 00:26:29,150
Let's go see her together sometime.

428
00:26:31,778 --> 00:26:32,779
Okay.

429
00:26:35,532 --> 00:26:38,243
Time goes by too fast when we're together.

430
00:26:38,326 --> 00:26:41,037
I have to go back to Seoul tomorrow.

431
00:26:43,039 --> 00:26:45,959
-You have so much work, right?
-Yeah, until the trial.

432
00:26:47,919 --> 00:26:50,004
Is there anything I can help you with?

433
00:26:53,842 --> 00:26:54,843
There is.

434
00:26:55,677 --> 00:26:58,346
Do you know what Baek Sang-gil
used to do a long time ago?

435
00:26:59,305 --> 00:27:01,307
-A long time ago?
-It was a long time ago.

436
00:27:01,891 --> 00:27:04,644
I found something suspicious
in his office.

437
00:27:09,733 --> 00:27:10,567
SEOUL BIRTH REGISTER

438
00:27:10,650 --> 00:27:14,154
We found this in your safe
while searching your office.

439
00:27:15,697 --> 00:27:20,660
It appears to be a register of births
in Seoul from May 1993 to 1994.

440
00:27:20,744 --> 00:27:21,953
You remember it, right?

441
00:27:23,204 --> 00:27:25,582
I grew up in an orphanage,
so I know how it goes.

442
00:27:26,166 --> 00:27:28,960
The illegal adoption of infants
and trafficking of newborns.

443
00:27:29,043 --> 00:27:31,421
Were you involved
in that sort of thing back then?

444
00:27:32,422 --> 00:27:35,133
I'm going to ask for life imprisonment
for you anyway.

445
00:27:35,759 --> 00:27:38,470
Adding one more crime
won't change your sentence,

446
00:27:38,553 --> 00:27:39,721
so why not just admit it?

447
00:27:39,804 --> 00:27:42,557
Adding one less crime
won't change my sentence either,

448
00:27:43,600 --> 00:27:46,144
so why not just stop digging?

449
00:28:04,454 --> 00:28:08,333
REHABILITATION

450
00:28:12,754 --> 00:28:17,467
It appears to be a register of births
in Seoul from May 1993 to 1994.

451
00:28:17,967 --> 00:28:19,093
You remember it, right?

452
00:28:35,985 --> 00:28:37,946
You're smoking a lot today.

453
00:28:38,488 --> 00:28:40,073
Do you have a lot on your mind?

454
00:28:44,202 --> 00:28:45,036
I guess so.

455
00:28:46,371 --> 00:28:48,081
They keep making me think about

456
00:28:49,666 --> 00:28:51,251
useless memories.

457
00:28:52,961 --> 00:28:54,754
It's all because of one guy.

458
00:28:55,922 --> 00:28:59,384
All of this happened
because he disobeyed me.

459
00:29:00,635 --> 00:29:03,179
Even the memories
that I didn't have to remember.

460
00:29:05,515 --> 00:29:08,142
I should've nipped that trouble
in the bud long ago.

461
00:29:16,401 --> 00:29:18,194
It's time to cut it down.

462
00:29:21,906 --> 00:29:24,242
The first trial
of former Gangju Mayor Ju Min-jong

463
00:29:24,325 --> 00:29:26,536
and Chairman Baek of Mirae Eden
will be held

464
00:29:26,619 --> 00:29:28,955
at the Seoul Eastern District Court
this morning.

465
00:29:29,038 --> 00:29:31,666
The prosecution is being led
by Prosecutor Go Ji-won.

466
00:29:33,001 --> 00:29:36,963
Furthermore, considering the antisocial
charges that have been uncovered,

467
00:29:37,046 --> 00:29:39,132
we seek 15 years' imprisonment
for Ju Min-jong

468
00:29:39,215 --> 00:29:43,052
and life imprisonment for Baek Sang-gil.

469
00:29:47,807 --> 00:29:49,183
Here, just a moment!

470
00:29:57,400 --> 00:29:59,277
Please say a few words!

471
00:30:07,911 --> 00:30:11,331
THE LATE JANG HYE-SU

472
00:30:12,457 --> 00:30:13,333
Mom.

473
00:30:14,876 --> 00:30:16,669
You've been watching everything, right?

474
00:30:18,129 --> 00:30:21,341
I'm sorry for disappointing you until now.

475
00:30:23,384 --> 00:30:24,385
But…

476
00:30:26,763 --> 00:30:28,348
I like how things are now.

477
00:30:31,059 --> 00:30:32,477
Now I'm truly…

478
00:30:35,563 --> 00:30:36,648
happy.

479
00:31:01,839 --> 00:31:04,258
You did a great job
getting through a big case.

480
00:31:05,134 --> 00:31:08,805
It's a shame because it seems like
there are still more crimes to uncover.

481
00:31:09,639 --> 00:31:12,809
They're such old cases
that many of them lack any evidence.

482
00:31:14,060 --> 00:31:14,936
Let's take it slow.

483
00:31:15,019 --> 00:31:16,020
Prosecutor!

484
00:31:18,314 --> 00:31:20,441
Baek Sang-gil escaped
the prison transport van.

485
00:31:21,609 --> 00:31:22,819
What the hell do you mean?

486
00:31:31,411 --> 00:31:33,079
EUN-SAE, HONG DO-YEOP, KIM GANG-ROK

487
00:31:37,834 --> 00:31:38,960
Sir!

488
00:31:41,212 --> 00:31:43,256
-Hurry up.
-What's going on?

489
00:31:43,756 --> 00:31:45,675
-How come you're…
-Baek Sang-gil escaped.

490
00:31:49,971 --> 00:31:50,805
Yeah.

491
00:31:51,472 --> 00:31:52,390
You're okay, right?

492
00:31:52,473 --> 00:31:53,599
Yeah, I'm okay.

493
00:31:53,683 --> 00:31:57,186
I'm under government protection,
and Violent Crimes is heading to Gujin.

494
00:31:57,812 --> 00:31:58,646
Here?

495
00:31:58,730 --> 00:32:01,524
If he escaped to hide or to stow away,
that'd be some relief.

496
00:32:01,607 --> 00:32:04,944
But if he escaped to get revenge,
then Taffy Village could be a target.

497
00:32:05,028 --> 00:32:06,988
Just be careful until then.

498
00:32:07,071 --> 00:32:09,282
I'll join you as soon as things
are settled here.

499
00:32:11,617 --> 00:32:15,038
Nothing suggests
that Baek Sang-gil is headed here.

500
00:32:15,121 --> 00:32:17,874
We're just preparing
for the worst-case scenario.

501
00:32:18,374 --> 00:32:19,459
Don't get scared yet.

502
00:32:20,501 --> 00:32:21,461
Okay.

503
00:32:26,424 --> 00:32:27,258
And Grandma?

504
00:32:39,979 --> 00:32:41,939
What's all that noise?

505
00:32:43,107 --> 00:32:43,941
Okay.

506
00:33:52,093 --> 00:33:54,679
-What about Jang Tae-ha?
-The boys are looking for him.

507
00:34:08,568 --> 00:34:10,486
What is it? Is she not picking up?

508
00:34:10,987 --> 00:34:13,573
No. I can't reach Song-wol either.

509
00:34:14,115 --> 00:34:15,575
GRANDMA

510
00:34:16,617 --> 00:34:17,451
Grandma.

511
00:34:17,535 --> 00:34:18,369
It's been a while.

512
00:34:20,163 --> 00:34:23,457
If you bring the police and make a fuss,
the old woman dies.

513
00:34:27,086 --> 00:34:28,129
Come alone.

514
00:34:28,629 --> 00:34:30,840
No. Don't come! You can't come here!

515
00:34:30,923 --> 00:34:32,300
-Grandma, you okay?
-Tae-ha!

516
00:34:32,383 --> 00:34:33,551
Don't you dare come--

517
00:34:33,634 --> 00:34:34,844
Grandma!

518
00:34:34,927 --> 00:34:36,345
Grandma, can you hear me?

519
00:34:38,055 --> 00:34:40,516
Baek Sang-gil, you bastard.

520
00:34:46,397 --> 00:34:47,398
Sir.

521
00:34:49,317 --> 00:34:50,985
-Let's go around.
-There's no time.

522
00:34:53,237 --> 00:34:55,031
-You can't.
-Coach.

523
00:34:55,114 --> 00:34:56,199
Not alone.

524
00:34:56,991 --> 00:34:58,951
We need at least three for that many.

525
00:35:04,874 --> 00:35:06,918
Everyone, please don't get hurt.

526
00:35:34,946 --> 00:35:36,280
Jang Tae-ha!

527
00:35:42,536 --> 00:35:43,621
Fuck!

528
00:35:56,676 --> 00:35:57,551
Damn it!

529
00:35:58,052 --> 00:35:59,929
Man, this isn't easy.

530
00:36:53,274 --> 00:36:54,483
When she was alive,

531
00:36:54,567 --> 00:36:58,195
she was a mother
who would protect her child with her life.

532
00:36:59,655 --> 00:37:02,575
I'm sure she's protecting her child
from heaven too.

533
00:37:03,492 --> 00:37:05,911
You won't be able to touch Tae-ha.

534
00:37:06,495 --> 00:37:08,956
You won't touch him. Never!

535
00:37:20,634 --> 00:37:21,969
There's something

536
00:37:23,554 --> 00:37:25,598
in this world
that you can never win against.

537
00:38:20,027 --> 00:38:21,195
Grandma!

538
00:38:23,155 --> 00:38:25,699
Why are you here? Why did you come?

539
00:38:25,783 --> 00:38:28,119
-Grandma, I'm here. You're okay now.
-Why would you…

540
00:38:28,202 --> 00:38:29,829
What are you going to do?

541
00:38:32,915 --> 00:38:33,833
It's okay now.

542
00:38:33,916 --> 00:38:35,209
-Be careful.
-It's okay.

543
00:38:35,292 --> 00:38:37,002
-It's okay.
-Good heavens.

544
00:38:38,379 --> 00:38:39,380
Oh my goodness.

545
00:39:09,952 --> 00:39:12,872
First off, your favorite things are
boxing and gochujang stew.

546
00:39:13,456 --> 00:39:16,041
I've just made it a lot.

547
00:39:16,125 --> 00:39:17,293
Because someone likes it.

548
00:39:46,113 --> 00:39:47,781
OUR STICKY LOVE

549
